class StreamingCryptoService:
    """============================================================================
    Streaming Crypto Service - Multi-Part and Message-Based Operations
    ============================================================================

    This service provides stateful, session-based cryptographic operations:
    - Multi-part Init/Update/Final (PKCS#11 streaming pattern)
    - Message-based AEAD (PKCS#11 v3.1 C_EncryptMessage/C_DecryptMessage)
    - Dual-function operations (simultaneous digest+encrypt, sign+encrypt)

    All operations are identified by a SERVER-GENERATED operation_id returned
    by the *Init response; clients pass it to every subsequent call.

    SESSION LIFETIME: Sessions hold server-side state. Implementations MUST
    enforce an idle-session TTL (expired sessions fail with
    CRYPTO_ERROR_OPERATION_EXPIRED), and clients SHOULD call CancelOperation
    when abandoning a session. See messages/session.proto.

    WHEN TO USE THIS vs CryptoService:
    CryptoService:          Stateless, single request/response. Use for
    individual operations (document encryption, etc.)
    StreamingCryptoService: Stateful, multi-step sessions. Use when:
    - Data doesn't fit in memory (multi-part streaming)
    - Many messages share one key setup (message-based AEAD)
    - PKCS#11 interop requires Init/Update/Final pattern

    ==================== Multi-Part Encryption ====================
    """

